Kamalie vibe and runs (@kamalie-vibe: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @ws-kamalie-games) {
## Desired experience

A quiet, spare, unpredictable mossy labyrinth viewed straight down in 2D. A small white circle is the central body. Dark green flat floor, another flat green for walls, brown sticks and simple bushes. Pixelated hard edges; no textures, decorative detail, HUD, buttons, inventory screen, skill bar or in-game menu. The things on screen communicate the world.

Each run starts without powerups from earlier runs. Discovery, customization, freedom of builds, dexterity and the player's experience supply progression. Dungeons, enemy types and weapons eventually come from authored generation rules rather than a fixed sequence. Randomness remains constrained by playable reachability and readable physical behavior.

Objects are either responsive to player controls or passive. Activation expresses a thing's physical behavior continuously. A stick is swung or thrust by the player; it does not trigger a canned skill animation. Things wear and break, affecting other things where contact happens.

## Planned work

- [x] Keep all persistent progression free of mechanical power advantages.
- [x] Reset carried items, attachments and damage at the start of a new run.
- [x] Carry the current build forward between levels within the same run.
- [x] Express interaction and damage through world geometry without a HUD.
- [ ] Playtest how simple physical parts produce distinct useful builds.
}
